{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 only guarantees polynomial BDD size for the read-once fragment but explicitly concedes BDD blow-up outside that fragment. The problem context demands that any proposal preserve polynomial cost for the semantics as stated, not merely for a syntactic restriction. Because the grounded extension can encode arbitrary defense conditions (including non-read-once formulas), there exist inputs where the BDD representation is exponentially large, violating the polynomial-cost guarantee required by the problem.","target":"604dc1f3880a2ecbdb4b8b6122184b502c2777646f70de45003d378fe14e2f66"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002's Horn encoding with a rule of the form accepted(X) :- not attacked_by_undefeated(X) introduces negation-as-failure that is not genuinely Horn. Standard Horn logic is definite and monotonic, so encoding the non-monotonic, fixed-point nature of the skeptical grounded semantics requires either stratified negation or auxiliary predicates that do not correspond to a least model in the Horn sense. The least model of a definite Horn program is monotonic and cannot directly represent a semantics where the acceptance of a conjecture depends on the non-acceptance of its attackers. The target itself acknowledges this ('may not preserve the exact grounded semantics unless carefully stratified'), meaning the proposal as written does not preserve the existing semantics guarantee, a core requirement of the problem.","target":"8e0f95c69421b331c8ce105f6f802756765ea89528480002ec920c0383bf987b"}]}